  "worked_solution": "First, we find ${g}^{\u2032}(t)$ and $\u2016{g}^{\u2032}(t)\u2016:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{\u2032}(t) & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-3t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2})\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e83{t}^{2}-3,\\,6t\u27e9 \\\\ \u2016{g}^{\u2032}(t)\u2016 & =\\sqrt{(3{t}^{2}-3)^{2}+(6t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{t}^{4}-18{t}^{2}+9+36{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{t}^{4}+18{t}^{2}+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(3{t}^{2}+3)^{2}} \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\u2016{g}^{\u2032}(t)\u2016\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(3{t}^{2}+3)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =({t}^{3}+3t){|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =(8+6)-(1+3) \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
